+Independent verification of the supplied proof, 2026-10-22, at revision
+8fd3d1ab48fbd4fba4acc4720674b8be1ea1db35 (Claude, independent verifier).
+
+Inspected: specs/CLAIM-delivery.md, specs/CLAIM-delivery/proof.md, the
+imported records CLAIM-exclusive and CLAIM-failover with their proofs and
+verifications, verification/deployments.md, verification/README.md, and
+verification/reservation.smt2.
+
+Attacks performed:
+
+- Imported-claim conclusions, read exactly. CLAIM-exclusive concludes
+  exclusivity only "when mode is single-worker"; CLAIM-failover concludes
+  recovery only "when mode is multi-worker". Both pass verdicts cover those
+  conditional conclusions, not unconditional ones.
+- Case split over deployments. verification/deployments.md states mode is
+  exactly one of single-worker or multi-worker. In a single-worker
+  deployment only exclusivity is imported; in a multi-worker deployment only
+  recovery is imported. No deployment satisfies both antecedents, so the
+  proof's final step ("Both records have pass verdicts, so this deployment
+  supplies both") does not follow. It drops the mode qualifiers and smuggles
+  a premise that one deployment satisfies both modes, which the stated
+  deployment model rules out.
+- Alternative support. reservation.smt2 was rerun with Z3 5.3.1 (both
+  obligations `unsat`). It discharges a 0..1 invariant for an abstract
+  reservation count only. It is not cited by the proof, is not tied to any
+  mode or to the worker API, and says nothing about recovery, so it does not
+  close the gap.
+- Falsification check. No production implementation or concrete delivery
+  counterexample is available (deployments.md), and the imported claims are
+  silent rather than contrary about the other mode. The gap is in the
+  argument; it does not show the claim false.
+
+Finding: the composition lemma is invalid. Lemmas 1 and 2 hold only under
+mutually exclusive modes, so the proof establishes neither conjunct of
+CLAIM-delivery for both modes together. Repair needs evidence of exclusivity
+in multi-worker mode or recovery in single-worker mode (or a deployment
+model where both imported antecedents hold); the claim wording is unchanged.
+
+Result: provisional
